{"name":"Carmel","hex":"#915f3d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carmel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A mountain range in Israel.","A female given name from Hebrew from the Roman Catholic epithet of Virgin Mary at Mount Carmel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carmel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carmel (biblical settlement)","blocks":[{"text":"Carmel was an ancient Israelite town in Judea, lying about 11.2 kilometres (7.0 mi) from Hebron, on the southeastern frontier of Mount Hebron. According to the Bible, Saul erected a victory monument in Carmel to memorialize his triumph over Amalek."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Southern_Palestine._Carmel._South_of_Hebron_LOC_matpc.00087.jpg/330px-Southern_Palestine._Carmel._South_of_Hebron_LOC_matpc.00087.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmel_(biblical_settlement)","wikidata":"Q2904870"},{"title":"Mount Carmel","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Carmel, also known in Arabic as Mount Mar Elias, is a coastal mountain range in northern Israel stretching from the Mediterranean Sea towards the southeast. The range is a UNESCO biosphere reserve. A number of towns are situated there, most notably Haifa, Israel's third largest city, located on the northern and western slopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Caiobadner_-_mount_carmel.JPG/330px-Caiobadner_-_mount_carmel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Carmel","wikidata":"Q185318"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Avigail-Tel-Maon-Karmil-623.jpg/500px-Avigail-Tel-Maon-Karmil-623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Avigail-Tel-Maon-Karmil-623.jpg/1280px-Avigail-